<Page title="How we compare AI tools" description="The process behind every ToolVerdict comparison: how we choose criteria, where prices come from, how we pick a winner and how often we re-check.">
  <p>Every comparison follows the same steps, so verdicts are consistent across articles.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Start from the job.</strong> We list the tasks people actually use a category for, such as summarising a long PDF, fixing a failing test or making a poster with legible text, and judge tools on those, not on feature counts.</li>
    <li><strong>Check facts against primary sources.</strong> Prices, plan limits and features come from each vendor's own pricing pages and documentation, which every article links under "Sources we checked".</li>
    <li><strong>Name a pick for each use case.</strong> "It depends" isn't an answer. Each article names one tool per job and explains why in one sentence.</li>
    <li><strong>Date everything.</strong> Each article shows when it was last updated and when prices were last checked.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Where we've run a tool ourselves on real tasks, the article includes a "What we saw in testing" section with what we observed.</p>
  <h2>How often we update</h2>
  <p>We review each comparison at least every 90 days, and soon after a major model or pricing change.</p>
</Page>
